    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nHello!\n\nIn my setup, I remap the escape key outside of nvim. Since the last system upgrade, the escape key when remapped does not work anymore at all inside vim. I investigated and found the following:\n\nDue to my remapping, the escape key press and release fire immediately without delay, so nvim receives them inside one buffer. However, `handle_raw_buffer` returns early, when an \"1b\" = escape byte is found. What's left, is then processed in the callback `tinput_timer_cb`. However, the next \"1b\" = escape for the key release then causes the `handle_raw_buffer` function inside the callback to return early, and the remaining key presses are lost.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse keyd with `overload` to remap ESC key, open vim and press remapped key.\n\nSample keyd config, remapping ESC (press and release) to CAPSLOCK and SHIFT (press + other key) to CAPSLOCK, too.\n```\n[ids]\n\n*\n\n[main]\n\ncapslock = overload(shift, esc)\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSame behavior as in the last release, never had any issue in the past.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1558+g8d5ebdf986-dirty\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKonsole\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\npacman",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
