        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "However it doesn't really make sense for libtermkey to interpret this as a release event with an <kbd>Alt</kbd> modifier... This seems to fix the problem:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/nvim/tui/termkey/termkey.c b/src/nvim/tui/termkey/termkey.c\nindex 77b65bc075..387464f59f 100644\n--- a/src/nvim/tui/termkey/termkey.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/tui/termkey/termkey.c\n@@ -912,6 +912,12 @@ static TermKeyResult peekkey_simple(TermKey *tk, TermKeyKey *key, int force, siz\n \n     switch (metakey_result) {\n     case TERMKEY_RES_KEY:\n+      if (key->event == TERMKEY_EVENT_RELEASE) {\n+        (*tk->method.emit_codepoint)(tk, b0, key);\n+        key->event = TERMKEY_EVENT_PRESS;\n+        *nbytep = 1;\n+        return TERMKEY_RES_KEY;\n+      }\n       key->modifiers |= TERMKEY_KEYMOD_ALT;\n       (*nbytep)++;\n       break;\n```",
            "created_at": "2026-09-08T01:08:27Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41763#issuecomment-5577532205",
